<PageTitle>Curriculum | Miss Mary's Little Lambs</PageTitle>
<article class="information-page">
    <h1>Curriculum Approach</h1>
    <p>At Miss Mary’s Little Lambs, my curriculum is thoughtfully guided while remaining flexible and responsive to each child’s needs. Rather than following a rigid, one-size-fits-all program, lessons are intentionally designed and adjusted based on student interests, developmental readiness, and daily observations.</p>
    <p>I believe young children learn best through meaningful experiences, play, and connection. Each week is carefully planned to include a balance of:</p>
    <ul><li>Early literacy (phonics, language development, and pre-reading skills)</li><li>Foundational math concepts through hands-on learning</li><li>Fine and gross motor development</li><li>Social-emotional growth and relationship building</li><li>Creative expression through art, music, and imaginative play</li><li>Nature-based exploration and curiosity-driven learning</li></ul>
    <p>Our curriculum evolves alongside the children—allowing for deeper engagement, natural curiosity, and a genuine love of learning to flourish.</p>
    <p>Influenced by play-based and developmentally appropriate practices, my approach supports the whole child—academically, socially, and emotionally.</p>
</article>
